    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class (the other two are helpers). The full suite is green.\n\nThe change is complete. Summary of what I implemented:\n\n- **`ValidateRegistrationDate`** (function class) \u2014 reads the request body via `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`; if a `registrationDate` is supplied and is after `LocalDate.now()`, it throws `FutureRegistrationDateException`. A null date is left untouched (the field remains optional).\n- **`FutureRegistrationDateException`** (checked exception) \u2014 carries the offending date and a descriptive message.\n- **`FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler`** + its escalation YAML \u2014 responds **400** with `{\"error\": \"...\"}`, mirroring the existing `InvalidPostcode` pattern.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `validateRegistrationDate` step among the other body-level 400 validations (after `validatePostcode`, before the 409/429 business checks and before `resolveRegistrationDate`), so a future date is rejected before it's rolled forward to a business day or counted against the daily limit.\n\nEach piece has a single responsibility and reuses the established endpoint conventions rather than folding the check into the existing `ResolveRegistrationDate`. The full test suite passes.",
